SingularityNET Omega
https://github.com/singnet/Omega
Copyright SingularityNET Foundation (CHE-358.649.107)
Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

  Omega's own NOTICE records that, effective 2026-07-22, SingularityNET
  Foundation relicensed the project from the MIT License to Apache-2.0.
  Releases prior to that date remain available under MIT.

  Tested at commit ee0618a293ec3662a32b10b09c6cbb073f59d6b2
  (describes as v0.1.19-141-gee0618a).

  MODIFICATIONS (Apache-2.0 section 4(b)). StickerBook's derived Omega role
  images (including jev/Dockerfile.jev and llm/Dockerfile.omega-llm) make the
  following changes to an unmodified upstream Omega image. None are committed
  to Omega; they exist only in locally built derived images.

    1. entrypoint.sh - the final exec interpolated "$*" into a `sh -c`
       string, so any configuration value containing a space was word-split
       and silently truncated to its first word. Replaced with the quoting
       pattern upstream already uses earlier in the same file. This is a bug
       fix, and is described in jev/EXPERIMENT.md.
    2. config/config.yaml and config/plugins.yaml are replaced, to select
       this experiment's provider, channel and finite-loop settings.
    3. /opt/nginx/nginx.sh is replaced with a no-op and the nginx config
       template removed, because the credential gateway is a separate
       container here.
    4. Unused channel and provider modules are deleted from the role images
       (including Telegram, Slack, IRC, Mattermost, WebSocket, and providers
       not needed by that role), so removed capabilities are absent rather
       than merely unconfigured.
    5. Role-specific config/plugin manifests replace the broad upstream
       runtime surface. OmegaLLM and OmegaJev are built as separate roles.
    6. OpenShell-derived role images run through StickerBook's non-root,
       environment-scrubbing entrypoint rather than the legacy in-agent
       credential proxy.

  Additions (this project's own code, MIT licensed, layered into derived
  images as applicable):
  providers/jev.py, providers/jev_core.py, providers/sb_bridge.py,
  channels/jevconsole.py, plugins/jevskills/, runtime/omega/stickerbookrpc.py,
  runtime/omega/stickerbookrpc.metta, llm/omega_llm/providers/stickerbook_llm.py,
  llm/omega_llm/config/, and the StickerBook authority-kernel integration.

  See docs/TOOLS-AND-MODIFICATIONS.md for the role-by-role rationale and
  verification status.

